<title>CHINA: Shanghai Commodity Exchange changes timetable.</title>
<headline>Shanghai Commodity Exchange changes timetable.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Shanghai Commodity Exchange will change its trading timetable from January 2, 1997, an exchange official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The revision was ordered by the China Securities Regulatory Commission, the country's top regulator, which wants all China's 14 futures exchanges to have the same trading timetable, analysts said.</p>
<p>Following is the new timetable, to take effect from January 2, 1997:</p>
<p>    0900 - 1000 (0100-0200 GMT)   plywood</p>
<p>    1010 - 1130 (0210-0330 GMT)   plywood, rubber</p>
<p>    1330 - 1500 (0530-0700 GMT)   plywood</p>
</text>
